      "result": "TCG icount installs get_virtual_clock but no set_virtual_clock callback. Qtest installs both. cpus_set_virtual_clock is a no-op if the callback is absent."
    },
    {
      "file": "util/qemu-timer.c:701",
      "result": "qemu_clock_advance_virtual_time repeatedly calls the optional setter and timer handlers until the clock reaches dest. With TCG icount paused inside MMIO and no working setter, it cannot by itself advance to a future time or model a CPU bus stall. Calling arbitrary timer handlers from that context also lacks a demonstrated reentrancy contract."
    },
    {
      "file": "docs/devel/tcg-icount.rst",
      "result": "Instruction counting is explicitly not cycle-accurate. MMIO restores unexecuted budget and uses a single-instruction translation to obtain current icount. The docs do not provide a timed bus-stall API."
    },
    {
      "file": "accel/tcg/icount-common.c:293",
      "result": "The existing warp path applies idle/runstate/replay and sequence-lock rules; it is not evidence that a device callback may edit clock bias."
    }
  ],
  "recommendation": "Keep atomic MMIO reference timing explicit. Do not call qemu_clock_advance_virtual_time from the new MMIO callback as a simulated stall. A later conservative CPU/PL scheduler needs its own proven event/budget/IRQ contract.",
